# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Urban Beauty project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version latest)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Placed `<SpeedInsights />` component within the `QueryClientProvider` wrapper
- Component is positioned after the `ReactQueryDevtools` component for optimal placement

## Implementation Details

This is a **Vite + React** project, so I followed the official Vercel documentation's React-specific instructions:
- Fetched the latest quickstart guide from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Used the React integration path (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`)
- Placed the component at the app root level for global performance tracking

The `SpeedInsights` component will automatically:
- Track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP)
- Send performance metrics to Vercel's Speed Insights dashboard
- Work seamlessly in production environments deployed to Vercel

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build successful: `npm run build` completed without errors
✅ Linter passed: No new linting errors introduced in App.jsx
✅ Dependencies installed: package-lock.json properly updated
✅ Code follows existing patterns: Maintained project's import organization and component structure

## Next Steps

To view Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Speed Insights dashboard in the Vercel project settings
3. After some visitor traffic, performance metrics will be available

